-- erwartet: N270 allein
-- **A bare store to an `atomic` has no form -- every store to one is a `publishstmt`.**
--
-- `AT = w;` on `atomic AT : u32 relaxed` used to check clean and emit `AT = w;`
-- over `_Atomic uint32_t AT` -- a plain store, which C treats as `seq_cst` while
-- the declaration said `relaxed`, and which the C model (`C-SPEICHERMODELL.md`
-- §1c) makes stuck. Lowering the bare store to an explicit
-- `atomic_store_explicit` is no fix either: the store is where the payload
-- promise stands (`publishes { … }` / `publishes nothing`, held by V001-V004),
-- and an explicit store without one would carry the pairing past the checker
-- in silence. So the checker refuses the bare store with N270 ALONE -- and
-- `cc` still accepts the emitted C, which is why this probe says `allein`:
-- the checker is the only guard on this form.
module gift::bare_store_to_atomic {

atomic AT : u32 relaxed;

impl fn schreibe(w : u32)
    effects { writes AT }
    costs   <= 4 ops
{
    AT = w;
}

}
